# Kernel paths for CoCo's gated self-improvement: the files an automated
# improvement loop must never change without the kernel owner's review
# (workflows, evals and their guard, tests, installers, scripts, and the
# loop's own code, caps and proposal schema).
# Changes here need review from the kernel owner, whose credentials are not on
# any machine that runs the improvement loop. The ruleset on main enforces
# "require review from code owners". Everything else follows the normal review rule.

/.github/                         @cococyracto
/.githooks/                       @cococyracto
/AGENTS.md                        @cococyracto
/docs/rules.md                    @cococyracto
/evals/                           @cococyracto
/tests/                           @cococyracto
/install.sh                       @cococyracto
/bin/                             @cococyracto
/adapters/                        @cococyracto
/Formula/                         @cococyracto
/scripts/                         @cococyracto
/skills/skill-evolution/scripts/  @cococyracto
/skills/skill-evolution/references/ @cococyracto
/skills/skill-evolution/state/     @cococyracto
/skills/skill-evolution/SKILL.md   @cococyracto
/skills/team-gate/                @cococyracto
/skills/arch-index/scripts/       @cococyracto
/skills/arch-index/references/    @cococyracto
/skills/arch-index/templates/     @cococyracto
/skills/arch-index/SKILL.md       @cococyracto
/commands/team/                   @cococyracto

# The loop's code (skill-evolution/scripts), its caps and proposal schema
# (skill-evolution/references) and the other rule-enforcing code and the rules it
# loads (all of team-gate, which has no SKILL.md; arch-index scripts,
# references and templates) are kernel. Listed folder by folder on purpose:
# CODEOWNERS has no negation, so owning a whole skill folder would also own its SKILL.md.
# The loop's ledger (skill-evolution/state) and the commands that call the gates
# (commands/team) are kernel too, as are the push gate and secret scan (.githooks),
# the rules of record (docs/rules.md, AGENTS.md) and the two SKILL.md files that define gate
# and guard rules (arch-index, skill-evolution); those are listed file by file.
# Other skill bodies (skills/*/SKILL.md) are deliberately NOT kernel: they are what the
# loop may propose edits to, through a reviewed PR that the off-machine checker
# scores.
